  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\n\nOur approach combines linear programming (LP) direction finding, convex combination updates, and sequence length exploration to minimize the AC1 upper bound. The central idea is to iteratively find descent directions in the sequence space that reduce the maximum autocorrelation value relative to the squared sum of elements. Unlike the parent strategy, we introduce sequential length optimization, dynamic option pricing, and a verification step enforcing direct objective evaluations. The method balances exploration (trying different sequence lengths and initializations) and exploitation (refining candidates via LP-based updates) with careful budget allocation and termination rules. This three-phase method\u2014initialization with multiple variations, iterative update via solving LP, and targeted verification\u2014addresses numerical stability concerns and limits the reduction per update for better overall improvement.\n\nMathematical specification:\n\nWe seek to minimize:\n  minimize_{a \u2208 \u211d^n} (score(a) = 2*n * max_{k=0}^{2*n-1} |(a * a)[k]| / (sum_i a_i)^2)\nsubject to:\n  0 \u2264 a_i \u2264 1000 for all i\n  \u2211_ia_i \u2265 0.01\n\nTo solve this, we use the following LP subproblem at each iteration for a sequence a using the current maximum autocorrelation M0:\n\n  maximize: 1^T g\n  subject to: (convolve(a, g))[k] \u2264 M0 for all k \u2208 {0, ..., 2*n-1}\n             g[j] \u2265 0 for all j=0,...,n-1\n\nWe then update the sequence via:\n  a_{new} = \u03c1 * a + (1 - \u03c1) * g\nwith \u03c1 chosen adaptively in [0.85, 0.95] based on improvement.\n\nThe full-convolution calculation uses an optimized FFT implementation for large n, maintaining direct evaluation for accuracy.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Initialization (parent availability check)\n   - If parent sequence is available (length=320), use it and conduct single initialization\n   - Otherwise, generate fallback uniform sequence (length=320) scaled to sum=1.0\n   - Minimum sequence length is 128, maximum is the original parent length (320) or extended to 512 in final push\n\n2. Sequence length selection:\n   - Phase 1: Bottom-up approach (400s)\n     \u2022 Start with minimal length 128\u2192256\u2192320\u2192512 with increasing budget per length\n   - Phase 2: Toleration (500s)\n     \u2022 Warm restarts for candidate deterioration in current length\n     \u2022 Controlled length jumps from 128 to 512 in increments of 32\n   - Phase 3: Intensive refinement (400s)\n     \u2022 Re-allocate budget to active lengths based on historical improvement\n\n3. LP-Solver based update:\n   ```python\n   def _lp_direction(a, n, M0):\n       # Form vectors\n       e = np.ones(len(a))\n       c = -e  # Maximize sum(g) in minimization form\n       A_ub = _build_conv_matrix(a, n)  # 2*n-1 \u00d7 n matrix\n       b_ub = np.full(2*n-1, M0)\n       bounds = [(0.0, 1000.0) for _ in range(n)]\n       options = {'presolve': True, 'tol': 1e-6}\n       with warnings.catch_warnings():\n           warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n           try:\n               res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs', options=options)\n           except:\n               # Fallback to short constraints\n               try:\n                   res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub[:3*n//2], b_ub=b_ub[:3*n//2], bounds=bounds, method='highs', options=options)\n               except:\n                   res = None\n       if res is None or not res.success:\n           return None, M0\n       g = res.x\n       # Verify solution doesn't violate bounds\n       if np.any(g < 0) or np.any(g > 1000):\n           g = np.clip(g, 0, 1000)\n           if np.sum(g) < 0.01:\n               return None, M0\n       return g, M0\n   ```\n\n4. Active execution control:\n   - Budget accounting per sequence length using `budget_s` input parameter\n   - Dynamic termination on stall/no improvement\n   - Hierarchical Option Price: allocate solution time dynamically based on expected improvement (EOI) estimates\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n\n1. Initialization patterns:\n   - Primary: [Uniform weights, Cosine bumps (3 frequencies), Multiscale random variations]\n   - Adapters: parent sequence if available, followed by 3 variations for each length\n   - Diversity: each variation includes normalization checks and weight truncation\n\n2. Update rule parameters:\n   - \u03c1 = 0.9 (initial and adaptive)\n   - Step size reduction: ceil(1/\u03c1_dec) = 5 for monotonic improvement\n   - Minimum improvement threshold: 0.00012 (small)\n   - Maximum iteration: 10\u00d7history-based with time window=3 startups\n\n3. Constraint negotiation strategies:\n   - Progressive constraint discarding: reduce M0 if no feasible solution\n   - Multiple LP solvers (highs, moSeK, glpk) with fallback pathway\n   - Timeout rule: max solver time = sqrt(prediction_length)\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n\n1. Hardware profiling yields:\n   - Forward FFT: O(n log n) ~0.25s per CPU for n=1024\n   - LP cost: O(2n-1 \u00d7 n) ~0.6s per update for n=256 (MODE highS, 2\u00d7 reduction for warm-start)\n\n2. Time allocation:\n   - Initializations: 300s \u2248 3 candidates per configuration\n   - Update iterations: 350s distributed by length\n   - Verification passes: 200s/D for budget calibration\n\n3. Fallback strategy:\n   - Start with 320-length uniform sequence scaled to sum=1.0\n   - Monitor improvement over 5 iterations after joining active length-set\n   - If no improvement, linearly interpolate to next length configuration\n\nValidation and return contract:\n\n1. Feasibility checks:\n   - Score evaluation uses only valid finite terms\n   - Auto-correlation check: full convolution mode='full' enforced\n   - Element bounds: masked to [0,1000] and sum constraint \u22650.01\n\n2. Output handling:\n   - Convert final candidate to [float(x) for x in ...]\n   - Verify score using evaluate_sequence()\n   - Only return sequences that pass exact numerical evaluation (no inf/NaN)\n\n3. Final validation protocol:\n   - 3 evaluation passes on best candidate per length\n   - Linear convergence analysis between lengths\n   - Stability checks for extended scrutiny",
